# Archived changes are immutable evidence: this repo's rule is that a dated artifact takes a
# dated correction LINE and is never rewritten. `lint-staged` runs `prettier --write` on every
# staged `*.md`, so without this entry the pre-commit hook (live since C10X-43 Phase 4) would
# reformat archived evidence wholesale the moment a correction line is appended to it — 116 of
# these files are prettier-dirty today, so the diff would be the whole file rather than the one
# line, and "verify the correction by diff shape" would stop being possible.
#
# Scoped to `archive`, deliberately NOT to `context/**`: a live `context/changes/` folder is a
# working document that should reach `/10x-archive` already normalised. Freezing it only once it
# is archived is what makes "the archive is immutable" a property of the tooling rather than of a
# reviewer's attention.
#
# Prettier 3 reads this file ALONGSIDE `.gitignore` rather than replacing it, so nothing already
# ignored becomes visible. Consequence to state rather than leave implicit: `npm run format` no
# longer touches the archive, by design.
context/archive/**
